R4.2: Any roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked.
R4.3: Administrators must update their credentials after Emergency mode ends.

KEY CONCEPTS AND ENTITIES
==========================
- User: An entity with a security clearance and possibly administrator status.
- Administrator: A user with High clearance and administrative privileges.
- Role: A set of permissions, possibly delegated, and may have mutual exclusion constraints.
- Delegated Role: A role temporarily granted to a user, subject to clearance and time constraints.
- System Object: An object with a classification level (High, Medium, Low).
- Request: An action submitted by a user, affecting one or more objects, classified by the highest object classification.
- Clearance Level: Security level assigned to users and objects (High, Medium, Low).
- Emergency Mode: A special system state with modified authorization and request processing rules, triggered by two administrators.
- Emergency Privileges: Special, temporary capabilities granted to administrators during Emergency mode.
- Mutual Exclusive Roles: Roles that cannot be held by the same user simultaneously except during Emergency mode.
- Mode: The current operational state of the system (Normal or Emergency).
- Credential Update: The requirement for administrators to update authentication information after Emergency mode.

