- During Emergency mode, the system may process high-classification requests out of FIFO order and concurrently.
- During Emergency mode, users may hold roles that are otherwise mutually exclusive.
- Emergency privileges granted to administrators must be temporary and revoked at the end of Emergency mode.
- All roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked upon its conclusion.
- Administrators are required to update their credentials after Emergency mode ends.
- The transition out of Emergency mode is mandatory and must occur after the fixed time elapses.
