=== MODEL IMPROVEMENT GUIDANCE ===
- On line 97 (in the ExistingSystem fact), correct the let-binding for the request clearance check.
- Alloy 6 let-binding syntax is either:
    let var = <expr> | <single expression>
  or (for a block of statements):
    let var = <expr> { <block of statements> }
- The current code:
    all r: Request |
        let cl = maxClass(r.affected) | {
            cl in Clearance and clToInt(cl) <= clToInt(r.requester.clearance)
        }
  is invalid because "|" and "{" should not be used together.
- FIX: Remove the curly braces and use a single "|" expression:
    all r: Request |
        let cl = maxClass(r.affected) |
            cl in Clearance and clToInt(cl) <= clToInt(r.requester.clearance)
  OR, if multiple statements are needed, use only curly braces:
    all r: Request |
        let cl = maxClass(r.affected) {
            cl in Clearance
            clToInt(cl) <= clToInt(r.requester.clearance)
        }
  But in Alloy, facts must be a single boolean expression, so the first (no braces) form is almost always correct here.

