[LESSON]: Syntax errors related to let-binding in Alloy 6 are frequent. Alloy 6 requires "let x = expr { ... }" for block scope, or "let x = expr | ..." for single-expression scope, but not both. Always check Alloy 6 grammar before applying let-binding fixes. Do not mix "|" and "{}" in let-bindings.
